{"ref":"BDB, חֵ֫לֶף","hw":"חֵ֫לֶף","html":"† I. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">חֵ֫לֶף</span></big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>exchange</strong>, only cstr., as prep. <em>in return for</em> <strong>(</strong>so <span dir=\"rtl\">חֲלַף</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܚܠܳܦ</span>, common in Aramaic e.g. <a data-ref=\"Genesis 4:23\" href=\"/Genesis.4.23\">Gn 4:23</a> 𝔗 𝔖 for Heb. <span dir=\"rtl\">תַּחַת</span><strong>)</strong>—<span dir=\"rtl\">ח׳ עֲבֹדֶתֶם (עֲבֹדַתְכֶם)</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 18:21\" href=\"/Numbers.18.21\">Nu 18:21</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 18:31\" href=\"/Numbers.18.31\">31</a> (both P).","next":"BDB, חֵ֫לֶף²","prev":"BDB, חָלַף"}